IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-interpretation`
IMPORT `g2-readings`
IMPORT `g3-fixtures`
IMPORT `g4-tests-fixtures`
IMPORT `g5-interpretation`
IMPORT `g6-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g8-tests-fixtures`
IMPORT `g9-interpretation`
IMPORT `int-readings`

-- int-tests-readings: the readings of the fleet (int-readings.l4, generated) are the readings each group takes, field by field, and IP33 and IP35 are one value each.
-- Each expected value is a statement about the group's own named value (its "favoured" or "default" reading), which that group's FRAGMENT says is the reading taken.

§ `The readings of the fleet`

GIVETH A `Interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
`G1 as the group names it` MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2`
GIVETH A `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
`G2 as the group names it` MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
GIVETH A `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
`G3 as the group names it` MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`
GIVETH A `Interpretation of Articles 11 and 12`
`G4 as the group names it` MEANS `the default reading`
GIVETH A `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
`G5 as the group names it` MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
GIVETH A `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
`G6 as the group names it` MEANS `the readings taken`
GIVETH A `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`
`G7 as the group names it` MEANS `the favoured interpretation`
GIVETH A `Interpretation of Articles 26 to 36`
`G8 as the group names it` MEANS `the favoured interpretation`
GIVETH A `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
`G9 as the group names it` MEANS `the favoured interpretation`

#ASSERT `Int the reading of Articles 1 and 2` EQUALS `G1 as the group names it`
#ASSERT `Int the reading of Articles 3 to 7` EQUALS `G2 as the group names it`
#ASSERT `Int the reading of Articles 8 to 10` `the calendar year` EQUALS `G3 as the group names it`
#ASSERT `Int the reading of Articles 11 and 12` EQUALS `G4 as the group names it`
#ASSERT `Int the reading of Articles 13 and 14` `the calendar year` EQUALS `G5 as the group names it`
#ASSERT `Int the reading of Articles 15 to 20` `calendar months` EQUALS `G6 as the group names it`
#ASSERT `Int the reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` `calendar months` EQUALS `G7 as the group names it`
#ASSERT `Int the reading of Articles 26 to 36` `calendar months` EQUALS `G8 as the group names it`
#ASSERT `Int the reading of Schedules 1 and 2` `calendar months` EQUALS `G9 as the group names it`

#ASSERT `Int the readings of the fleet are consistent` `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`
